## WHAT?
- Remove signal‑forwarding handlers before re‑emitting the child’s terminating signal.
- Add a fallback exit path to avoid hanging if self‑signaling is ignored.
- Add a regression test for signal‑exit semantics and make the stub binary shebang PATH‑independent.

## WHY?
- The wrapper could exit 0 or hang after a child process dies by signal, breaking scripts/CI that expect 128+signal exit codes.

## HOW?
- Track signal handlers and unregister them prior to self‑signaling.
- Compute a fallback exit code from the signal number.
- Add a node:test regression test using a stub vendor binary.

## BEFORE
```js
["SIGINT", "SIGTERM", "SIGHUP"].forEach((sig) => {
  process.on(sig, () => forwardSignal(sig));
});

if (childResult.type === "signal") {
  process.kill(process.pid, childResult.signal);
} else {
  process.exit(childResult.exitCode);
}
```

## AFTER
```js
const signalHandlers = new Map();

function registerSignalHandler(signal) {
  const handler = () => forwardSignal(signal);
  signalHandlers.set(signal, handler);
  process.on(signal, handler);
}

function stopSignalForwarding() {
  for (const [signal, handler] of signalHandlers.entries()) {
    process.off(signal, handler);
  }
}

["SIGINT", "SIGTERM", "SIGHUP"].forEach(registerSignalHandler);

if (childResult.type === "signal") {
  stopSignalForwarding();
  const signalNumber = osConstants.signals[childResult.signal];
  const fallbackExitCode =
    typeof signalNumber === "number" ? 128 + signalNumber : 1;
  const fallbackTimer = setTimeout(() => {
    process.exit(fallbackExitCode);
  }, 250);
  try {
    process.kill(process.pid, childResult.signal);
  } catch {
    clearTimeout(fallbackTimer);
    process.exit(1);
  }
} else {
  process.exit(childResult.exitCode);
}
```

## TESTS
- [x] `node --test codex-cli/tests/signal-forwarding.test.mjs`
- [x] Manual: stubbed vendor binary + SIGTERM → exit_status=143
- [x] Rerun after branch update (2026-01-27): `node --test codex-cli/tests/signal-forwarding.test.mjs`, manual stubbed vendor binary + SIGTERM → exit_status=143

